abstract: >
  BOS Platform is the software realisation of a protocol-first staged
  bioconversion architecture backing Paper 1 (J Clean Prod, in
  preparation). The paper's bench-scale relay couples Tenebrio molitor
  (Module 1, upstream conditioning) to Protaetia brevitarsis (Module 3,
  downstream conversion) via a declared aqueous handover layer
  (Module 2, the aerobic kernel), with a Signal-API / Control-API
  interface standardising the inter-stage handover; black soldier fly
  (Hermetia illucens) is treated only as a comparison benchmark in
  paper §4.3, not as a primary executor. The relay is exercised on
  distillers' grains as the principal substrate and extended to
  tobacco straw, traditional Chinese medicine (TCM) residue, and
  primary-clarifier sludge under matched-boundary accounting. The
  software exposes a five-endpoint causal inference layer
  (/api/v1/causal/identify, /estimate, /refute, /mediation,
  /sensitivity) that operationalises the paper's pre-registered
  in-silico analyses. The mediation endpoint implements Pearl/Rubin
  counterfactual mediation (NDE/NIE decomposition) over the
  Signal-API -> kappa -> SER pathway (~70% proportion mediated). The
  sensitivity endpoint operationalises the paper's Gamma-bound >= 1.5
  falsification gate via VanderWeele-Ding E-value (primary, DoWhy 0.14
  EValueSensitivityAnalyzer) with a self-implemented Chinn-VWD
  fallback and an additional Cinelli-Hazlett robustness value branch
  for linear-bound analysis. A LangGraph agent orchestrates the five
  endpoints; a paper SHA-256 pin gate keeps the software-paper audit
  chain intact.
